  "defects": [
    "Late unique packets arriving after a report never canceled their previously reported cumulative loss. Their receipts also failed to offset new loss in the current report interval.",
    "An expired packet could set an aliased receive-bitmap slot and hide a newer missing packet before its report. Exact reported-loss tags alone did not prevent this."
  ],
  "repair": [
    "Track exact sequence identities for reported missing packets in a fixed8192-slot array. A unique late receipt within that history cancels the marker once and corrects cumulative loss.",
    "Subtract uniquely recovered receipts from newly missing packets for interval loss, saturating at zero; consume that credit at every report, including an interval with no sequence advancement.",
    "Expire tags as forward progress reuses slots. Arrivals outside the retained history cannot mutate aliased receive bits; the existing jitter/timestamp update still runs."
  ],
